course: dictionary
lesson: 12092
title: Coming together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Coalesce means to come together and join into one bigger thing. Coalesced is its past form, so it tells you the joining has already happened. Read the words around it for clues: «Tiny drops of water coalesced on the cold window, and they ran down as one big drop.» The drops joined. They did not stay apart.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try your meaning in the sentence: «Tiny drops of water joined together on the cold window, and they ran down as one big drop.» It still makes sense, so joined together is a good meaning for coalesced.
explain: Scientists use coalesced to explain how things form. «Over millions of years, dust and gas coalesced to make a star.» The tiny bits did not stay separate. They came together to make one thing. Historians use it for groups too: «The small villages coalesced into one town.»
fact: Coalesced means came together and joined into one bigger thing.
fact: Coalesce is the base word, and coalesced is its past form, so the joining has already happened.
fact: In science, coalesced can describe things that have merged, as in «coalesced droplets».
fact: «Coalesced» is used to explain how stars, planets, raindrops and bubbles were formed.
fact: A simple check: if you can swap in "joined together" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
exercise: «Tiny drops of water coalesced on the cold window.» What does coalesced mean? | Dried up and disappeared | Fell far apart | *Came together and joined into one bigger drop | Froze into small ice cubes
exercise: «Over millions of years, dust and gas coalesced to make a star.» What happened to the dust and gas? | They became hot and cold | They got lost in space | *They came together and joined into one thing | They stayed apart
exercise: Find and copy the word that means joined into one: «The small villages coalesced into one town.» | town | villages | small | *coalesced
test: «Two small bubbles coalesced into one big bubble.» What does coalesced mean here? | Burst and vanished | Floated away slowly | *Joined together into one | Got bigger all by themselves
test: Scientists say a planet formed when small rocks coalesced. Which word is the past form of coalesce? | coalesce | coalescing | *coalesced | coalesces
exam: Which sentence uses coalesced correctly? | I coalesced my homework and went to bed | The cake coalesced in the oven | *The separate streams coalesced into one river | The dog coalesced and ran fast
